{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And this is the making of the menorah.</b> He mentioned that nothing like it was seen." "<b>Miksha [beaten work].</b> I have explained it." "<b>Yarekha [its base].</b> It refers to the shaft upon which it stands, for thus it is written: \"its base and a shaft.\"" "<b>Perkha [its blossom].</b> It is known, and the skilled craftsman had no power to make it thus, were it not that HaShem showed it to Moses in the vision of prophecy." "<b>So he made.</b> It reverts to Moses, and the meaning is in the commandment, likewise: \"and you shall make a menorah of gold.\"" "And the reason for juxtaposing the portion of the Levites is to show that Aaron is engaged in kindling the lamp, and in the rest of the service the Levites assist him and stand before him to do whatever he commands."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:48.168152799Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}